DISPUTE CORRESPONDENCE - CONTRACTOR'S LETTERS

Letter No. JNC/2019/089
Date: 15.12.2019

To:
The Superintending Engineer,
Water Resources Department, Rajasthan

Subject: Geological Surprise - Unexpected Rock Strata Encountered
Reference: Agreement No. WRD/PALI/SUKLI/DAM/2019/004

Dear Sir,

We refer to the site possession given on 01.09.2019. During foundation excavation for the
main dam wall, we have encountered Type III hard rock instead of Type I soft rock as per
the initial geo-technical report provided by WRD.

This unexpected geological condition requires:
- Additional drilling and blasting operations
- Heavy machinery (rock breakers, excavators with rock bucket)
- Specialized explosives and blasting charges
- Extended timeline for foundation completion

Per CPWD GCC Clause 12 (Physical Conditions) and FIDIC Sub-Clause 4.12, this is a
geological surprise and should be treated as a compensable variation.

We request WRD to immediately depute a technical team to verify the geological
conditions and approve the additional cost claim.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Jal Nirman Constructions Ltd.
Project Manager

***

Letter No. JNC/2020/112
Date: 01.04.2020

To:
The Superintending Engineer,
Water Resources Department, Rajasthan

Subject: COVID-19 Force Majeure Notice - Complete Work Suspension
Reference: Agreement No. WRD/PALI/SUKLI/DAM/2019/004

Dear Sir,

In light of the nationwide lockdown announced by the Government of India due to
COVID-19 pandemic, we hereby issue this Force Majeure Notice under CPWD GCC Clause 65.

All construction activities at the Sukli Dam site are suspended from 25.03.2020 until
further government notification. This includes:
- All labor and workforce
- Heavy machinery and equipment
- Material supply chains
- Technical and supervisory staff

This suspension is beyond our control and constitutes an Event of Force Majeure.
We request WRD to:
1. Grant Extension of Time for the duration of the lockdown.
2. Compensate for idle establishment costs during this period.
3. Adjust the completion date accordingly.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Jal Nirman Constructions Ltd.
Director

***

Letter No. JNC/2021/189
Date: 15.06.2021

To:
The Superintending Engineer,
Water Resources Department, Rajasthan

Subject: Monsoon Force Majeure - Cofferdam Breach
Reference: Agreement No. WRD/PALI/SUKLI/DAM/2019/004

Dear Sir,

We regret to inform that the upstream cofferdam has breached due to unprecedented
heavy rainfall on 12.06.2021 (450mm in 24 hours). This is an Act of God event beyond
reasonable prediction.

Damage assessment:
- Complete loss of cofferdam structure
- Flood damage to partially constructed foundation
- Silting of excavation work
- Damage to equipment at site

Immediate remedial action required:
- Complete cofferdam reconstruction
- De-silting and re-excavation
- Foundation repair and strengthening
- Equipment recovery and repair

Estimated additional cost: ₹3.20 Crore
Estimated delay: 3 months

Per CPWD GCC Clause 65 (Force Majeure), this event qualifies for compensation
and Extension of Time.

Yours faithfully,
For M/s. Jal Nirman Constructions Ltd.
Director